          dealing: "Four cards dealt to each player clockwise. Remainder forms the stock to dealer's right (stock version), or use four cards of one rank per player with no stock.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Collect four cards of the same rank, then take a spoon. Do not be the last player without a spoon.',
          gameplay: "Players pass one card face down to their left-hand neighbour at a time (and in the stock version the dealer draws from the stock while the player to dealer's right discards to a pile). Passing continues until someone collects four of a kind. That player takes a spoon from the center; as soon as one spoon is taken, all other players may grab a spoon. One fewer spoon than players, so one player loses the deal. Loser gets a letter (e.g. S-P-O-O-N) or is eliminated; remove one spoon per eliminated player.",
          keyRules: [
            'Pass exactly one card at a time to the left; never hold more than four cards.',
            'First to collect four of a kind takes a spoon; then everyone may grab a spoon.',
            'Last player without a spoon loses the deal.',
            'When stock is exhausted, shuffle the discard pile to form a new stock.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep your eyes on the spoons, not just your cards. If you see movement in the center, grab first, ask questions later. Don't hold disparate cards; focus on one rank early (e.g., if you have two 5s, discard everything else to find the other two 5s).",
          intermediate: "The 'Sneaky' Grab: If you get 4 of a kind, quietly take a spoon without anyone noticing. Continue playing/passing cards with one hand while holding the spoon. Watch the chaos unfold as others realize slowly.",
          advanced: "The 'Fake' Reach: Reach towards the spoons to make everyone panic-grab. Rules often penalize this (e.g., you lose a life if you touch a spoon without 4 of a kind). Use with caution.",
          tips: [
            'Remove sharp objects (watches/rings).',
            'Use durable spoons (plastic or metal).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
